dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6618319Z error[vulnerability]: Buffered application data sent to outer server after ECH rejection
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6618530Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/om-openmath/om-openmath/Cargo.lock:328:1
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6618613Z     │
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6618872Z 328 │ rustls 0.23.45 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6619182Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6619497Z     │
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6619653Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0347
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6619893Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0347
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6620170Z     ├ When a server rejects Encrypted Client Hello (ECH), the client completes the
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6620413Z       handshake using the outer ClientHello and authenticates the server against the
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6620627Z       ECH config's `public_name`. At the end of that handshake, rustls encrypted and
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6624872Z       queued any application data buffered via `ClientConnection::writer()` *before*
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6624989Z       queueing the `ech_required` alert.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6625063Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6625171Z       The application correctly receives
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6625418Z       `Error::PeerIncompatible(ServerRejectedEncryptedClientHello)`, but the next
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6625611Z       `write_tls()` call (needed to send the alert) also sends the buffered
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6625912Z       application data. Plaintext meant for the inner server therefore goes to the
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6626126Z       client-facing server named by `public_name`.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6626250Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6626592Z       That server is authenticated, so this is not exploitable by an unauthenticated
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6627157Z       party, but it violates RFC 9849 section 6.1.6, which requires the client to
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6627508Z       abort with `ech_required` "before sending any application data to the server".
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6627636Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6627799Z       This affects only clients that:
