dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6643590Z error[vulnerability]: Unauthenticated ServerHello can downgrade later connections to classical key exchange
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6643964Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/om-openmath/om-openmath/Cargo.lock:328:1
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6644055Z     │
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6644323Z 328 │ rustls 0.23.45 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6644625Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6644710Z     │
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6644828Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0349
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645045Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0349
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645308Z     ├ The client recorded the server-selected key exchange group for each server
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645514Z       name when processing the ServerHello, before the server was authenticated.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645721Z       This record is used to predict which key share to send in future ClientHellos
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645808Z       to that server name.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6645883Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6646084Z       A network attacker can answer one connection attempt with a ServerHello
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6646297Z       selecting X25519, and then close the connection. Later ClientHellos for that
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6646492Z       name carry only an X25519 key share, while `supported_groups` still lists
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6646695Z       X25519MLKEM768 first. If the genuine server accepts that share rather than
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6646900Z       sending a HelloRetryRequest for its preferred hybrid group, the handshake
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647113Z       completes with classical-only key exchange and no error. This persists for as
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647264Z       long as the entry stays in the client's session store.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647334Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647550Z       The impact is loss of post-quantum confidentiality for affected connections
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647721Z       ("harvest now, decrypt later"). There is no key compromise and no
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647818Z       authentication bypass.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6647898Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648081Z       The following are not affected:
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648160Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648392Z       - connections to servers which send a HelloRetryRequest for their preferred group,
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648562Z       - clients with resumption disabled (as nothing is stored), and
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648647Z       - other server names.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648722Z       
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6648817Z       This behaviour is discussed in
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6649558Z       [draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction-01.html#name-security-considerations),
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6649724Z       so the practical impact depends largely on server policy.
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6649949Z     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/pull/3355
dependencies	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T13:42:32.6650166Z     ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.46 (try `cargo update -p rustls`)
